From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 20:20:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: cedrus: jpeg: quiet the refusal of undecodable images

The JPEG decoder parses the image itself and refuses what the engine
cannot decode (greyscale, non-interleaved scans, 16-bit tables, images
larger than the capture format) or what does not parse at all. Each
refusal wrote two error lines to the kernel log, "unsupported JPEG: ..."
or "failed to parse JPEG header: -22" and "Failed to setup decoding
job: -22". The image comes from userspace, which gets its buffer back
with V4L2_BUF_FLAG_ERROR: a damaged MJPEG stream, or a stateful client
feeding the stateless decoder, flooded the log at the frame rate (30
pairs in half a second from GStreamer's v4l2jpegdec on this board).

Make the JPEG refusals debug messages and rate-limit the generic setup
failure message, which stays an error for the codecs whose parameters
come from validated controls.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_dec.c  |  4 ++--
 drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_jpeg.c | 15 +++++++++------
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_dec.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_dec.c
@@ -217,8 +217,8 @@
 
 	error = ctx->current_codec->setup(ctx, &run);
 	if (error)
-		v4l2_err(&ctx->dev->v4l2_dev,
-			 "Failed to setup decoding job: %d\n", error);
+		dev_err_ratelimited(dev->dev,
+				    "Failed to setup decoding job: %d\n", error);
 
 	/* Complete request(s) controls if needed. */
 
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_jpeg.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_jpeg.c
@@ -223,9 +223,13 @@
 	return tables[index].start;
 }
 
+/*
+ * The image comes from userspace, which gets the buffer back with the error
+ * flag: a refused image is a debug message, not a kernel log line per frame.
+ */
 static int cedrus_jpeg_fail(struct cedrus_ctx *ctx, const char *what)
 {
-	v4l2_err(&ctx->dev->v4l2_dev, "unsupported JPEG: %s\n", what);
+	dev_dbg(ctx->dev->dev, "unsupported JPEG: %s\n", what);
 	return -EINVAL;
 }
 
@@ -276,8 +280,7 @@
 
 	ret = v4l2_jpeg_parse_header(src_vaddr, size, &header);
 	if (ret < 0) {
-		v4l2_err(&dev->v4l2_dev,
-			 "failed to parse JPEG header: %d\n", ret);
+		dev_dbg(dev->dev, "failed to parse JPEG header: %d\n", ret);
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
@@ -359,9 +362,9 @@
 	 * buffer, and its MCU-padded width the line stride.
 	 */
 	if (width > dst_fmt->width || height > dst_fmt->height) {
-		v4l2_err(&dev->v4l2_dev,
-			 "JPEG of %ux%u does not fit the %ux%u capture format\n",
-			 width, height, dst_fmt->width, dst_fmt->height);
+		dev_dbg(dev->dev,
+			"JPEG of %ux%u does not fit the %ux%u capture format\n",
+			width, height, dst_fmt->width, dst_fmt->height);
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
